  "hypotheses": [
    "A factory-only verifier can derive GENESIS, INCARNATION_GENESIS, SUCCESSOR, REFRESH, or NO_CHANGE from exact retained capture and structural read-set bytes without accepting a caller-selected publication decision.",
    "Publication-time trust can verify immutable committed inventory at the retained decision time while a separately live recovery trust verifies the finalized anchor and freshness at recovery time, provided root, key-ring history, authority namespaces, monotonic anchor state, exact freshness receipt digests/times, and independently configured trust-anchor paths are bound.",
    "Committed branches can deterministically reconstruct the exact N+6 mutation set, digest projections, mutation fixed point, audit/outbox/commit self-digests, DeviceRecord-set digest, and resolved four-authority vector, while NO_CHANGE remains an exact zero-write branch.",
    "These byte relationships remain component premises until authentic authority transport, repository CAS and transaction clocks, atomic visibility, outbox delivery, target mapping, and end-to-end execution are independently observed."
  ],
