  "limitations": [
    "The publication read receipt, authority bytes, trusted times, configured authority paths, verifier nonces, and repository rows are caller or adapter inputs. The component verifies their retained relationships but does not directly fetch them from an independent product authority.",
    "Dual-trust verification binds the exact publication and recovery freshness receipt digests, verified/expires times, independently expected trust-anchor paths, root set, key-ring history prefix, authority namespaces, and monotonic trust-anchor state. It does not prove direct authority path ownership, fresh nonce transport, HSM/KMS custody, or an external service's linearizable current read.",
    "The locally closed CAS-result shape and repository transaction rows are caller-supplied. They do not prove a real SERIALIZABLE transaction, four-authority CAS execution, trusted commit clock, commit durability, or atomic visibility.",
